# Privacy Policy — AutoGerente

_Last updated: November 16, 2026_

AutoGerente shows what your vehicle costs and reminds you of maintenance and document deadlines. It
works without an account and without a server: **what you log stays on your phone**. This policy
explains what the app uses, why, and what happens on the free plan, which shows ads.

## 1. What stays on your phone

Vehicles, fill-ups, expenses, income, services, reminders, documents, receipt photos and your
preferences are stored only on the device. Receipt photos are kept in a private app folder and do not
appear in your gallery. We have no server, create no account and receive no copy of this data. The
app never asks for a full license plate, VIN, national ID or other personal document: at most the
last digit of the plate or the registration month, when your region's calendar uses it.

## 2. Permissions

Each permission is requested only when you use the feature, and the app keeps working if you deny it.
The app does not use location, contacts or the microphone.

| Permission | What for |
|---|---|
| Notifications and alarms | Maintenance, document and logging reminders at the time you choose, also after a restart. |
| Camera | Taking a photo of a service or expense receipt. The photo stays in the app. |
| Photos | Picking a receipt photo from your gallery (the app only sees the photos you pick) and saving the image you share to your gallery. |
| Files | Saving and opening the backups, the spreadsheet and the history you export or receive. |

## 3. Backup, spreadsheet and passing the history on

Backups, the spreadsheet, the PDF report and the history file are files **you** create and send
wherever you want (email, messages, another app). The Premium automatic backup is kept in a folder on
the phone itself. Once you send a file, the service you chose handles it under its own policy. The
history file can have a 4-digit code that prevents opening it by mistake.

## 4. Ads (free plan)

The free plan shows ads from **Google AdMob**. To show and measure ads, Google may collect the
device's advertising ID, the IP address (and the approximate location derived from it), device and
system information, and ad interactions.

- Where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland), the app asks
  for your consent first through Google's consent platform, and you can change it later.
- On iPhone, the system asks whether the app may track you across apps; without permission, the
  advertising ID is not used.
- **Premium** has no ads.

How Google uses this data: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>.

## 5. Purchases

Subscriptions and the lifetime purchase are processed by **Google Play** or the **App Store**. We do
not receive your payment details; the app only checks whether Premium is active.

## 6. Children

The app is not made for children and does not knowingly collect data from children under 13.

## 7. Your rights and deleting your data

Because the data stays on your phone, you control it: delete entries in the app, use "Erase all
data" in Settings › Backup & data, or uninstall the app. Advertising data follows Google's
policy and your device settings (reset or turn off the advertising ID).

